# Spec 11.3.1 / 12.2: `@` names an own field's payload (an Array field's
# descriptor), a parameter or an address slot, never an Array element's
# storage; that pointer needs an explicit adapter. Emitting it produced the
# address of a temporary copy (0c, run_l2_message_root element_address).

fn: first_address () int
    []: int buf 3
    buf[0]: 7
    return: @ buf[0]
end: first_address
